Python does not have a built-in way to forbid inheritance. However, you can use a metaclass to achieve this effect.
Here's an example of how to create a metaclass that prevents inheritance:

{% highlight "python" %}
class NoInheritanceMeta(type):
    def __init__(cls, name, bases, dct):
        for base in bases:
            if isinstance(base, NoInheritanceMeta):
                raise TypeError(f"Inheritance from {base.__name__} is forbidden")
        super().__init__(name, bases, dct)

class Parent(metaclass=NoInheritanceMeta):
    pass

# This will raise a TypeError
class Child(Parent):
    pass
{% endhighlight %}